[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[Variation "Englund Gambit: Main Line"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Character "tactical,gambit"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pin"]
[Themes "accept-the-pawn,block-with-bishop"]
[Kind "gambit"]

1. d4 e5 { The Englund Gambit: Black gives a pawn for quick play and some traps. } 2. dxe5 { Take it. The gambit is not sound, and the tricks only work if White goes wrong. } 2... Nc6
(2... d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 4. Nc3)
3. Nf3 { Defends e5 and develops. } 3... Qe7
(3... Bc5 4. Nc3)
(3... Nge7 4. Nc3)
4. Bf4 { Defends e5 a second time with the bishop that is already outside the pawn chain. } 4... Qb4+
(4... d6 5. exd6)
5. Bd2 { The right block. Other blocks lose a piece (see the traps) because the queen on b4 also hits the bishop on f4. } 5... Qxb2
(5... Qe7 6. Nc3)
6. Nc3 { Brings the knight out and clears the first rank. If the queen takes the rook on a1, the white queen takes it back. } 6... Bb4
7. Rb1 { Attacks the queen, which has to leave b2 with the rook on a1 now safe. } 7... Qa3
8. Rb3 { Attacks the queen again with tempo and keeps her away from the b-file. } 8... Qa5
9. e4 { Takes the centre now that White is a pawn ahead and nearly fully developed. } 9... Nge7
10. a3 { Asks the bishop on b4 what it wants to do. After ...Bxc3 Bxc3 the bishop pair and the extra pawn are safe. Plan: Bd3, castle, and keep the extra pawn. } *
